on":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120241","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120241","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120241.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120241.patch","merged_at":"2026-06-15T13:56:42Z"},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #120214\r\n\r\n- #119871 caused two regressions in addition to #119979.\r\n\r\n1. The key acquisition range in cases where playback is slowed down by `stretch_time_scale` has become broken\r\n2. `start_offset` no longer functions in `stretch_time_scale`; This prevents the adjustment of the start position for the period of time-adjusted walking cycles\r\n\r\n- I will partially revert #119871 with keeping some lines for the start-end section to prevent the recurrence of the issue with #118101\r\n\r\n**Revert:**\r\n\r\n- The change to `cur_len` definition and change usage of `anim_size` causes issue 1, so this must be reverted\r\n- Removing `start_offset` from the time calculation causes issue 2, so this must be reverted\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n- I tested #119988 locally, and all tests passed except for the cases where `start_offset` is valid with stretched `custom_timeline`. The test cases for `stretch_time_scale` with `start_offset` in #119988 are based on the results from a regression in #119871, so the expected values of the tests are incorrect in the first place\r\n\r\nSimply put, what was needed for #119871 compared to #119846 was at most the handling for Backward at https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119871#discussion_r3336380354, as we discussed in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119846#pullrequestreview-4381786505.\r\n\r\ncc @chocola-mint \r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","htm